\* Normative Invariant Catalog (verified by explicit-state models):
\* [I01] (Crypto, Section 4.6, 27.1): Cipher suite is selected at most once and never mutates across migration, resumption, or rekey.
\* [I02] (Crypto, Section 7.5, 27.1): Every AEAD seal uses a strictly monotonic per-connection packet number; no (key, nonce) pair is ever reused.
\* [I03] (Wire, Section 5.2, 27.1): Outer header bytes are authenticated as exact AEAD AAD; any header mutation fails decryption before state change.
\* [I04] (Lifecycle, Section 20.1, 27.1): Application STREAM/DATAGRAM frames are never emitted or accepted outside key-bearing states.
\* [I05] (Transaction, Section 22.2, 27.1): Failed AEAD or malformed frame preflight mutates zero transport, replay, flow-control, or path credit state.
\* [I06] (Replay, Section 13.2, 27.1): Replay window bits below the sliding floor are cleared before window advancement to prevent modulo aliasing.
\* [I07] (Replay, Section 13.1, 27.1): ACK frames never imply cumulative delivery outside their explicit [low, high] intervals.
\* [I08] (Ledger, Section 13.3, 27.1): An ACK covering a packet number >= next_pn or a RESERVED/BURNED entry triggers ACK_RANGE_ERROR.
\* [I09] (Handshake, Section 7.6, 27.1): Server never transitions to ESTABLISHED before client FINISH MAC verifies; client never confirms before HANDSHAKE_DONE.
\* [I10] (Stream, Section 12.1, 27.1): Stream slot generation increments strictly upon retirement completion and halts at SLOT_EXHAUSTED (2^32-1).
\* [I11] (FlowControl, Section 12.4, 27.1): Emitted stream offset never exceeds send.limit and connTxUsed never exceeds connTxLim.
\* [I12] (Stream, Section 12.5-12.6): Stream final_size is bound at most once on send and receive halves; conflicting FIN/RESET offsets trigger FINAL_SIZE_ERROR.
\* [I13] (Stream, Section 21.1, 27.1): STREAM_RETIRE and RETIRE_ACK are emitted only when both local halves of the slot are terminal.
\* [I14] (Congestion, Section 14.1, 27.1): Each in-flight packet charges bytes_in_flight once on emission and releases at most once across ACK, LOST, or ABANDONED.
\* [I15] (PMTU, Section 15.3, 17.2): MTU_PROBE targets above 2*M clamp pacing token reservation to 2*M so binary search up to 4096B never deadlocks.
\* [I16] (Congestion, Section 15.1, 27.1): Congestion window halves at most once per recovery boundary ordinal.
\* [I17] (ECN, Section 15.4, 27.1): Decreasing or impossible peer ECN counters immediately transition path ECN state to ecnBroken and disable ECT(0).
\* [I18] (ECN, Section 15.4, 27.1): Any path migration or tuple change permanently disables sender ECN marking for the remainder of the connection.
\* [I19] (KeyRefresh, Section 19.1, 27.1): At most three epoch slots (PREV, ACTIVE, NEXT) exist simultaneously; epoch numbers increase by exactly +1.
\* [I20] (KeyRefresh, Section 19.4, 27.1): KEY_COMMIT is valid only when NEXT is staged with matching refresh_id and valid transcript MAC.
\* [I21] (KeyRefresh, Section 19.6, 27.1): Reaching the 2^32 hard packet-number limit in an epoch without key rotation immediately closes with AEAD_LIMIT_REACHED.
\* [I22] (KeyRefresh, Section 19.5, 27.1): PREV epoch keys are zeroized upon grace timer expiry and never seal outbound packets.
\* [I23] (Lifecycle, Section 20.3, 27.1): DRAINING, QUIESCING, and DEAD states never emit wire packets.
\* [I24] (Lifecycle, Section 20.1, 27.1): DEAD is an absorbing terminal state for all events.
\* [A01] (AsyncIO, Section 29.5, 34.1): An ACK covering a SUBMITTED packet waits for I/O acceptance rather than validating an unaccepted wire emission.
\* [A04] (AsyncIO, Section 29.5, 34.1): Rejected async send transitions SUBMITTED to BURNED and rolls back pacing/amplification charges while burning the PN.
\* [A08] (AsyncIO, Section 20.3, 34.1): Transition from QUIESCING to DEAD is blocked while any zero-copy or crypto I/O pin remains outstanding.
\* [M01] (Mobility, Section 17.3, 38.1): A fresh authenticated packet on a new tuple never validates or promotes that tuple without PATH_CHALLENGE/PATH_RESPONSE.
\* [M02] (Mobility, Section 17.3, 38.1): Unvalidated candidate output never exceeds 3*rxBytes or 3*rxPkts.
\* [M06] (Mobility, Section 17.2, 38.1): Transition to READY/ACTIVE requires both challenge token verification and bidirectional 1200-byte datagram proof.
\* [M07] (Mobility, Section 17.1, 38.1): At most one ACTIVE, one CANDIDATE, and one OLD path exist simultaneously.
\* [M09] (Mobility, Section 17.4, 38.1): A pre-cutover old-path packet (pn < cutover_pn) never reverses an accepted migration or re-promotes OLD.
\* [M15] (Parking, Section 35.4, 38.1): Repeated PARK_REQUEST or PARK_GRANT frames never extend the initially recorded lease expiry.
\* [M16] (Parking, Section 35.6, 38.1): Parking preserves all live streams, unread bytes, replay bitmaps, and key epochs.
\* [M17] (Parking, Section 35.8, 38.1): Waking never resumes bulk application TX before path readiness and credit backing are confirmed.
\* [M21] (Memory, Section 12.2, 38.1): Frames carrying stale or future stream generations never allocate state or mutate the active generation.

SafetyInvariants == TypeOK /\ TerminalAbsorptionOK
Spec == Init /\ [][Next]_vars
=============================================================================
